  "headline": "n*eps sweep (n 32-8192, eps 1-64, 20 cells): the release's own classifier (k -> inf limit of naive use) gains from a tree once n*eps >= 8192 for the non-private oracle tree and >= 32768 for the private per-dataset MST tree (all cells at and above, NLL); below ~2,000 every tree release is worse than plain feature-label margins. Private selection becomes informative near n*eps 2,000 and near-oracle by 8,000-33,000. Plain marginals keep a structural over-confidence of +0.075 to +0.087 at n*eps >= 32,768 that only the tree removes (noise-free TAN beats noise-free NB by 0.055-0.122 nats for n >= 128). At n*eps <= 128 the plug-in is far more over-confident than the PFN on k=1 rows (+0.321 to +0.412 vs +0.111 to +0.181), so bulk synthetic rows matter when k is large."
